{"duration_api_ms":444346,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"c279478b-7c14-4a2c-8ca4-8c8685926020","total_cost_usd":2.9217835999999995,"usage":{"input_tokens":198,"cache_creation_input_tokens":127763,"cache_read_input_tokens":9858583,"output_tokens":43447,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":7220},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":127763,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2411,"cache_read_input_tokens":143619,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1168},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4069,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004149,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":198,"outputTokens":43447,"cacheReadInputTokens":9858583,"cacheCreationInputTokens":127763,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.9176345999999995,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":7220,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":167,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Configured PostgreSQL 15 streaming replication across node1 (primary), node2, and node3 (standbys) on RHEL 7.9, secured with TLS using a cluster-specific CA, restricting replication connections to peers presenting CA-issued client certificates. All three nodes were restarted one at a time (standbys first, primary last) with quorum preserved throughout; each node's changed boot identity and full recovery of PostgreSQL service, replication, and data were verified.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Diagnosed and fixed RHEL7 repo issues: corrected $releasever mismatch (7Server vs 7) in PGDG repo baseurls, disabled EOL pgdg12/13 mirrors, installed EPEL-7 from Fedora archives to satisfy libzstd dependency, then installed postgresql15-server/contrib on node1, node2, node3\",\"Initialized PGDATA on node1 as the primary via postgresql-15-setup initdb\",\"Generated a dedicated cluster CA (postgres-cluster-ca) on node1; issued TLS server certs for node1/node2/node3 and a client cert (CN=replicator) for replication auth, all signed by that CA\",\"Distributed the CA cert, server certs, and replicator client cert to node2/node3 over SSH using the cluster keypair, with correct ownership/permissions under the postgres user\",\"Configured postgresql.conf on all nodes with ssl=on and node-specific ssl_cert_file/ssl_key_file/ssl_ca_file; set wal_level, max_wal_senders, max_replication_slots, hot_standby on node1\",\"Configured pg_hba.conf on node1 to accept replication connections only via hostssl with cert auth method scoped to node2/node3 IPs, implicitly requiring verify-full client cert validation against ssl_ca_file\",\"Opened firewalld port 5432/tcp on all three nodes\",\"Created the replicator role (REPLICATION LOGIN) and physical replication slots (node2_slot, node3_slot) on node1\",\"Ran pg_basebackup from node1 over TLS (sslmode=verify-full, client cert auth) to bootstrap node2 and node3 as standbys with primary_conninfo/primary_slot_name auto-configured\",\"Verified end-to-end replication: both standbys streaming async over SSL with client_dn=/CN=replicator; test rows written on primary appeared on both standbys\",\"Verified enforcement: a replication attempt without a client certificate was rejected by pg_hba\",\"Captured boot_id baseline on all nodes, then restarted node2, node3, and node1 sequentially (one at a time), confirming changed boot_id, service reactivation, replication reconnection, and data consistency after each restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"PostgreSQL streaming replication configured node1(primary)->node2,node3\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7f1e1b108dd145ab\",\"cmd-16385aab80ec4cd4\",\"cmd-d5d335e830c247d9\",\"cmd-b22725c5a5de4e45\"],\"summary\":\"pg_stat_replication on node1 shows node2 (10.100.34.11) and node3 (10.100.34.12) streaming async; test row inserted on primary appeared on both standbys\"},{\"requirement\":\"Replication traffic carried over TLS using a cluster-created CA\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d6d8aceb012c4b87\",\"cmd-1a54533b1b654cea\",\"cmd-9f8d60683eb847ea\",\"cmd-9454da5bdd064cc4\"],\"summary\":\"Created postgres-cluster-ca (ca.crt/ca.key) on node1; pg_stat_ssl joined to pg_stat_replication shows ssl=t and client_dn=/CN=replicator for both standby connections, both before and after the full restart sequence\"},{\"requirement\":\"Only peers presenting a CA-issued certificate are accepted for replication\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5888c604858744f8\",\"cmd-393033b9883e4a75\",\"cmd-0ff235863df242ec\"],\"summary\":\"pg_hba.conf restricts replication to hostssl+cert method scoped to node2/node3 IPs; a connection attempt without a client certificate was rejected (FATAL: no pg_hba.conf entry ... SSL encryption) while attempts presenting the CA-issued replicator cert succeeded\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 mandatory restart evidence\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a8d98b099a304c99\",\"cmd-6b5574d4ca244839\",\"cmd-16bf6429e1964e39\",\"cmd-851f95fb0f92464e\",\"cmd-a86c3b807a9748ca\",\"cmd-875c68ffdb264685\",\"cmd-f5e2d662d4b24017\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id d72bd4ec...; systemctl reboot issued; boot_id changed to 938def43...; postgresql-15 active, pg_is_in_recovery=f, both standbys reconnected streaming, and a post-restart test row replicated to node2 and node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 mandatory restart evidence\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a8d98b099a304c99\",\"cmd-9931370cd553442c\",\"cmd-03df7e60594545b5\",\"cmd-43cad0d98b424bb3\",\"cmd-69c68e9f07f8424d\",\"cmd-dd1c9347ecf041ca\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id d7a80301...; systemctl reboot issued; boot_id changed to ca95c822... with uptime 0 min; postgresql-15 active, pg_is_in_recovery=t, and node1 shows node2 reconnected streaming\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 mandatory restart evidence\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-30d00c63b40240f2\",\"cmd-07a2c63468ad4adb\",\"cmd-f6188a6174ff489e\",\"cmd-87a633f9e5834133\",\"cmd-284720796c52481c\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 73bafeef...; systemctl reboot issued; boot_id changed to 228d9c79... with uptime 0 min; postgresql-15 active, pg_is_in_recovery=t, and node1 shows node3 reconnected streaming\"},{\"requirement\":\"Quorum/independent recovery path preserved during restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6b5574d4ca244839\"],\"summary\":\"Only one node was restarted at a time; before restarting node1 (primary), both standbys were confirmed healthy and streaming, and node1 itself was only restarted after both standbys had already recovered from their own restarts\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured PostgreSQL 15 streaming replication across node1 (primary), node2, and node3 (standbys) on RHEL 7.9, secured with TLS using a cluster-specific CA, restricting replication connections to peers presenting CA-issued client certificates. All three nodes were restarted one at a time (standbys first, primary last) with quorum preserved throughout; each node's changed boot identity and full recovery of PostgreSQL service, replication, and data were verified.","actions_performed":["Diagnosed and fixed RHEL7 repo issues: corrected $releasever mismatch (7Server vs 7) in PGDG repo baseurls, disabled EOL pgdg12/13 mirrors, installed EPEL-7 from Fedora archives to satisfy libzstd dependency, then installed postgresql15-server/contrib on node1, node2, node3","Initialized PGDATA on node1 as the primary via postgresql-15-setup initdb","Generated a dedicated cluster CA (postgres-cluster-ca) on node1; issued TLS server certs for node1/node2/node3 and a client cert (CN=replicator) for replication auth, all signed by that CA","Distributed the CA cert, server certs, and replicator client cert to node2/node3 over SSH using the cluster keypair, with correct ownership/permissions under the postgres user","Configured postgresql.conf on all nodes with ssl=on and node-specific ssl_cert_file/ssl_key_file/ssl_ca_file; set wal_level, max_wal_senders, max_replication_slots, hot_standby on node1","Configured pg_hba.conf on node1 to accept replication connections only via hostssl with cert auth method scoped to node2/node3 IPs, implicitly requiring verify-full client cert validation against ssl_ca_file","Opened firewalld port 5432/tcp on all three nodes","Created the replicator role (REPLICATION LOGIN) and physical replication slots (node2_slot, node3_slot) on node1","Ran pg_basebackup from node1 over TLS (sslmode=verify-full, client cert auth) to bootstrap node2 and node3 as standbys with primary_conninfo/primary_slot_name auto-configured","Verified end-to-end replication: both standbys streaming async over SSL with client_dn=/CN=replicator; test rows written on primary appeared on both standbys","Verified enforcement: a replication attempt without a client certificate was rejected by pg_hba","Captured boot_id baseline on all nodes, then restarted node2, node3, and node1 sequentially (one at a time), confirming changed boot_id, service reactivation, replication reconnection, and data consistency after each restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"PostgreSQL streaming replication configured node1(primary)->node2,node3","command_ids":["cmd-7f1e1b108dd145ab","cmd-16385aab80ec4cd4","cmd-d5d335e830c247d9","cmd-b22725c5a5de4e45"],"summary":"pg_stat_replication on node1 shows node2 (10.100.34.11) and node3 (10.100.34.12) streaming async; test row inserted on primary appeared on both standbys"},{"requirement":"Replication traffic carried over TLS using a cluster-created CA","command_ids":["cmd-d6d8aceb012c4b87","cmd-1a54533b1b654cea","cmd-9f8d60683eb847ea","cmd-9454da5bdd064cc4"],"summary":"Created postgres-cluster-ca (ca.crt/ca.key) on node1; pg_stat_ssl joined to pg_stat_replication shows ssl=t and client_dn=/CN=replicator for both standby connections, both before and after the full restart sequence"},{"requirement":"Only peers presenting a CA-issued certificate are accepted for replication","command_ids":["cmd-5888c604858744f8","cmd-393033b9883e4a75","cmd-0ff235863df242ec"],"summary":"pg_hba.conf restricts replication to hostssl+cert method scoped to node2/node3 IPs; a connection attempt without a client certificate was rejected (FATAL: no pg_hba.conf entry ... SSL encryption) while attempts presenting the CA-issued replicator cert succeeded"},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart evidence","command_ids":["cmd-a8d98b099a304c99","cmd-6b5574d4ca244839","cmd-16bf6429e1964e39","cmd-851f95fb0f92464e","cmd-a86c3b807a9748ca","cmd-875c68ffdb264685","cmd-f5e2d662d4b24017"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id d72bd4ec...; systemctl reboot issued; boot_id changed to 938def43...; postgresql-15 active, pg_is_in_recovery=f, both standbys reconnected streaming, and a post-restart test row replicated to node2 and node3"},{"requirement":"node2 mandatory restart evidence","command_ids":["cmd-a8d98b099a304c99","cmd-9931370cd553442c","cmd-03df7e60594545b5","cmd-43cad0d98b424bb3","cmd-69c68e9f07f8424d","cmd-dd1c9347ecf041ca"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id d7a80301...; systemctl reboot issued; boot_id changed to ca95c822... with uptime 0 min; postgresql-15 active, pg_is_in_recovery=t, and node1 shows node2 reconnected streaming"},{"requirement":"node3 mandatory restart evidence","command_ids":["cmd-30d00c63b40240f2","cmd-07a2c63468ad4adb","cmd-f6188a6174ff489e","cmd-87a633f9e5834133","cmd-284720796c52481c"],"summary":"Baseline boot_id 73bafeef...; systemctl reboot issued; boot_id changed to 228d9c79... with uptime 0 min; postgresql-15 active, pg_is_in_recovery=t, and node1 shows node3 reconnected streaming"},{"requirement":"Quorum/independent recovery path preserved during restarts","command_ids":["cmd-6b5574d4ca244839"],"summary":"Only one node was restarted at a time; before restarting node1 (primary), both standbys were confirmed healthy and streaming, and node1 itself was only restarted after both standbys had already recovered from their own restarts"}]},"ttft_ms":1388,"type":"result","duration_ms":1056764,"uuid":"c4dee4ba-1356-4e1e-9bb4-b8c7bd756661","ttft_stream_ms":817,"time_to_request_ms":65,"first_content_frame_ms":1387,"queued_turn_count":0}
